Use `Files.list` to read the folder and `Files.move` to rename. `Files.move` throws `FileAlreadyExistsException` if the target exists (unless you pass `REPLACE_EXISTING`), so the no-overwrite rule is covered by default. The explicit `Files.exists` check lets you print a clear warning first.

```java
import java.io.IOException;
import java.nio.file.Files;
import java.nio.file.Path;
import java.nio.file.Paths;
import java.util.List;
import java.util.stream.Stream;

public class RenameJpeg {
    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {
        if (args.length < 1) {
            System.err.println("Usage: RenameJpeg <directory>");
            System.exit(1);
        }

        Path dir = Paths.get(args[0]);
        if (!Files.isDirectory(dir)) {
            System.err.println("Not a directory: " + dir);
            System.exit(1);
        }

        List<Path> files;
        try (Stream<Path> stream = Files.list(dir)) {
            files = stream
                    .filter(Files::isRegularFile)
                    .filter(p -> p.getFileName().toString().toLowerCase().endsWith(".jpeg"))
                    .sorted()
                    .toList();
        }

        int renamed = 0;
        int skipped = 0;

        for (Path file : files) {
            String name = file.getFileName().toString();
            String newName = name.substring(0, name.length() - 5) + ".jpg";
            Path target = file.resolveSibling(newName);

            if (Files.exists(target)) {
                System.err.println("Warning: " + newName + " already exists, skipping " + name);
                skipped++;
                continue;
            }

            Files.move(file, target);
            System.out.println(name + " -> " + newName);
            renamed++;
        }

        System.out.println("Renamed " + renamed + ", skipped " + skipped);
    }
}
```

Notes:

- `Files.list` is not recursive. Use `Files.walk(dir)` if you also want subfolders.
- The stream is opened in try-with-resources and collected to a list first. This closes the directory handle before you start renaming.
- `.toList()` needs Java 16 or newer, so it works on your Java 17.
- On a case-insensitive file system (Windows, default macOS), `photo.JPEG` and `photo.jpg` count as the same name. The `exists` check will then skip the file. That is usually what you want.
- There is a small gap between `exists` and `move`. For a manual tool this is fine, because `Files.move` still refuses to overwrite and throws instead. Catch `FileAlreadyExistsException` if other programs write to the folder at the same time.

