```python
import re
from html import escape

BLOCKED = ["guaranteed", "miracle", "cure", "100% free", "risk-free"]

# Only the rules this template uses.
PAGE_CSS = """
body { font-family: sans-serif; margin: 0; }
.product { max-width: 720px; margin: 2rem auto; }
.title { font-size: 1.6rem; }
.price { color: #1a7f37; font-weight: bold; }
.desc { line-height: 1.5; }
"""

# Compiled once. One pass over the text instead of one pass per blocked phrase.
_BLOCKED_RE = re.compile(
    r"\b(?:" + "|".join(re.escape(w) for w in sorted(BLOCKED, key=len, reverse=True)) + r")\b",
    re.I,
)
_SPACES_RE = re.compile(r"\s{2,}")
_SLUG_RE = re.compile(r"[^a-z0-9]+")
_SKU_RE = re.compile(r"[A-Z]{2}-\d{4,6}")


def clean_description(text):
    text = _BLOCKED_RE.sub("", text)
    return _SPACES_RE.sub(" ", text).strip()


def make_slug(title):
    return _SLUG_RE.sub("-", title.lower()).strip("-")


def valid_sku(sku):
    return _SKU_RE.fullmatch(sku) is not None


def render_product(p):
    if not valid_sku(p["sku"]):
        raise ValueError("bad sku: " + p["sku"])
    desc = escape(clean_description(p["description"]))
    slug = make_slug(p["title"])
    return (
        "<html><head>"
        '<link rel="canonical" href="/p/' + slug + '">'
        "<style>" + PAGE_CSS + "</style></head><body>"
        '<div class="product">'
        '<h1 class="title">' + escape(p["title"]) + "</h1>"
        '<div class="price">' + format(p["price"], ".2f") + "</div>"
        '<p class="desc">' + desc + "</p>"
        "</div></body></html>"
    )
```

**Green Notes**
- **Unused CSS removed** (reduces network and E): `.carousel`, `.carousel-item`, `.modal`, `.modal-open`, `.wishlist-btn` and `.badge-sale` are never used by this template. The CSS is inlined into every page, so each of the 40k pages carried those bytes. The page looks the same. Before you ship this, check that no other template reuses `PAGE_CSS`. https://patterns.greensoftware.foundation/development/media-and-code-efficiency/remove-unused-css
- **Regexes compiled once at module level** (reduces E): in Green Metrics Tool micro-benchmarks, a precompiled pattern used about 18% less CPU energy than inline `re.match` over 1,000,000 matches ([measurements](https://metrics.green-coding.io/compare-simple.html?ids=3827c15a-4295-44a4-8025-a07e8653ab7e,b7a9f0bd-c9e0-4b95-9bda-e8a96f38020c,f3e0434d-744b-41a0-a0cc-9bf00d80500d)). The gain is small because Python's `re` caches compiled patterns. It was never the real cost here.
- **One alternation instead of a loop of `re.sub` calls** (reduces E): the old code built five patterns per product and scanned the description five times. Now it is one pattern and one scan. Phrases are still matched case-insensitively and as whole words, and the longest phrase is tried first. The output is the same.
- **`fullmatch` replaces `^...$`:** a `$` also accepts a trailing newline, so `"AB-1234\n"` used to pass. `fullmatch` rejects it. That is stricter, so if your feeds can contain trailing newlines, strip the SKU before you validate it.

