**Green Notes**
- **Modern image formats** (reduces network): AVIF and WebP send fewer bytes than the 1.8 MB JPEG to every visitor of the page. The savings come from the smaller transfer, not from cheaper decoding.
  https://patterns.greensoftware.foundation/development/media-and-code-efficiency/serve-images-in-modern-formats
- **Encode at build time** (reduces E): in Green Metrics Tool micro-benchmarks, encoding 50 BMP images to AVIF used about 658 J against about 89 J for JPG, roughly 7× ([measurements](https://metrics.green-coding.io/stats.html?id=81a932bc-04da-443b-93cf-d4d8468de247)). Do this once in CI and cache the output files. Never do it per request.
