- **Name the columns, skip `log_output` and `artifact_json`** (reduces E, network): the database no longer reads, sends and decodes a full build log for every row in the list. In Green Metrics Tool micro-benchmarks on a 52-column table with large text columns, naming 10 columns instead of `SELECT *` used about 5.5× to 7× less CPU energy ([measurements](https://metrics.green-coding.io/compare-simple.html?ids=b7203ffe-39ae-4e84-bf85-998c9389ea46,4702c2ee-13d5-4d70-bcfe-31e193104a8e)). Your table is smaller, so treat that as a direction, not a prediction. The saving grows with the size of the skipped columns. https://patterns.greensoftware.foundation/development/data-handling/reduce-transmitted-data
