Review of our changelog page generator please. Diff only, no rewrite of the whole file. It turns the .md release notes into one static page, and release notes often have screenshots.

```javascript
#!/usr/bin/env node
const fs = require('fs');
const path = require('path');

const [, , srcDir, outFile] = process.argv;
const config = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(path.join(srcDir, 'site.json'), 'utf8'));

function escapeHtml(s) {
  return s.replace(/&/g, '&amp;').replace(/</g, '&lt;').replace(/>/g, '&gt;');
}

function renderLine(line) {
  let html = escapeHtml(line);
  for (const [name, url] of Object.entries(config.shortlinks)) {
    html = html.replace(new RegExp('\\b' + name + '-(\\d+)\\b', 'g'), `<a href="${url}$1">${name}-$1</a>`);
  }
  html = html.replace(/!\[([^\]]*)\]\(([^)]+)\)/g, '<img src="$2" alt="$1">');
  html = html.replace(/\*\*(.+?)\*\*/g, '<strong>$1</strong>');
  return html;
}

const files = fs.readdirSync(srcDir).filter((f) => f.endsWith('.md')).sort();
const out = ['<!doctype html><meta charset="utf-8"><title>' + config.title + '</title>'];
for (const f of files) {
  const lines = fs.readFileSync(path.join(srcDir, f), 'utf8').split('\n');
  out.push(`<section id="${path.basename(f, '.md')}">`);
  for (const line of lines) {
    if (line.trim() === '') continue;
    out.push('<p>' + renderLine(line) + '</p>');
  }
  out.push('</section>');
}
fs.writeFileSync(outFile, out.join('\n'));
```

**Workload:** script (static page generator), plus the page it produces

#### [Bug] Shortlink names go into the regex unescaped
- **Where:** `new RegExp('\\b' + name + '-(\\d+)\\b', 'g')`
- **Issue:** a name like `C++` or `v1.x` in `site.json` is read as regex syntax. It either throws or matches the wrong text.
- **Fix:** escape the name when you build the pattern (see diff).

#### [High] Every screenshot loads on page open
- **Where:** the `<img>` string in `renderLine`
- **Issue:** the page is one long changelog, so most screenshots are far below the fold. Every visitor still downloads all of them.
- **Fix:** add `loading="lazy"`.
- **Impact:** reduces network bytes and client work for each page view. The saving grows with the number of screenshots.

#### [Medium] Shortlink regexes are rebuilt for every line
- **Where:** the `for` loop in `renderLine`
- **Issue:** `new RegExp(...)` runs once per shortlink for every non-empty line, but the patterns never change. The engine caches compiled patterns, so the compile itself is cheap. You still pay for the object creation, string concatenation and cache lookup on each call.
- **Fix:** build the patterns once when the config is loaded.
- **Impact:** reduces E in the generator. It is small for a short changelog and grows with the number of lines times shortlinks.

#### [Low] Regex literals inside the function
- **Where:** the image and bold patterns
- **Issue:** V8 caches these too, so the gain is minor. Moving them to constants is only for consistency with the change above.

