**Green Notes**
- **Memoized label vectors** (reduces E): each request re-hashed every label, although the same few labels come back every time. Now each label is embedded once and later requests only do a map read.
- **Bounded cache:** labels come from the client, so the map stops growing at 1024 entries. Extra labels are just computed per request, like before.
- *Not applied:* caching `embed(in.Text)`. Input texts are mostly unique, so a cache would only add locking and memory.
- **Minified script** ([Minify web assets](https://patterns.greensoftware.foundation/development/web-performance/minify-web-assets)) (reduces network): comments and indentation no longer travel to every visitor. esbuild writes no source map here, so none is shipped.
- The script is now a separate file the browser fetches next to the page, so it costs one extra request. It also keeps the Go code free of JS in a string. Behavior and output of `/classify` are unchanged.

